# Explore Why DNA Must Repeat

A four-letter alphabet offers only $4^4=256$ possible four-mers. Start with the live threshold explorer and see how the sufficient bound $q^k+k$ changes with alphabet size and motif width.

{{interactive_demo:0}}

The underlying counting idea is the [pigeonhole principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigeonhole_principle): a word of length $m$ has $m-k+1$ windows, so $m\ge q^k+k$ supplies more windows than patterns.

{{visualization:2}}

## Find an explicit witness

The collision-search algorithm scans windows from left to right and remembers the first position of each block.

