{{demo:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal why decoding preserves the collision</summary>

At length $b^4+4$, two encoded four-mers are equal by pigeonhole counting. Applying the same decoder to corresponding symbols preserves equality. No injectivity assumption on the decoder is needed.

</details>

For broader background, see introductions to [combinatorics on words](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combinatorics_on_words) and [DNA sequencing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNA_sequencing). Empirical genome comparisons require a specified assembly, ambiguity policy, random model, and exact statistic; the deterministic thresholds here provide a baseline rather than an empirical estimate.
